# winoracle (12th Gen Intel Core i9-12900KF, Windows 10.0.26200.9457), 2026-10-11; the POPAD register
# rows (seeded EDI/ESI/EBP, stub set-up 2+15 bytes, hence ip=+17) re-measured twice on 2026-10-12.
# x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -O1 (first block) and i686-w64-mingw32-gcc -O1 (second block).
# A stack WRITE fault outside the guard (PUSH, CALL, PUSHF, ENTER, PUSHAD) is STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION --
# never STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW -- and undeliverable here (the dispatch frame would land in the same no-access
# page), so the process ends with 0xC0000005 (WER can take over 20 s to end it; the probe waits 120 s).
# A stack READ fault (POP, POPF, RET, RET imm16, POPAD, LEAVE) is delivered as STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION,
# [0]=0, [1]=the first inaccessible byte, at the instruction, with the STARTING stack pointer (ctxsp=+0) --
# even for LEAVE, whose RSP<-RBP step and pop fault as one instruction, and for POPAD after four successful
# pops. POPAD is not all-or-nothing, though: the registers popped before the faulting slot hold the slot
# values (popad partial: EDI/ESI/EBP = slots 0..2, 0x5107000n), while a fault on the first slot leaves the
# seeds (0x5EED000n).
64-bit, word 8, stub set-up 3 bytes (+3 with bp)
push r64        sp=B+8 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
push imm32      sp=B+8 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pushfq          sp=B+8 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
call rel32      sp=B+8 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
enter 16,0      sp=B+8 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
push r64 strad  sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pop r64         sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+3
popfq           sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+3
ret             sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+3
ret 8           sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+3
pop r64 strad   sp=B-4 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+3
leave           sp=B-64 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+6
32-bit, word 4, stub set-up 2 bytes (+2 with bp)
push r32        sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
push imm32      sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pushfd          sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
call rel32      sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
enter 16,0      sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
push r32 strad  sp=B+2 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pushad          sp=B+4 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pushad partial  sp=B+4104 undeliverable: process exit status c0000005
pop r32         sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+2
popfd           sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+2
ret             sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+2
ret 8           sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+2
pop r32 strad   sp=B-2 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+2
popad           sp=B+0 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+17
                  edi=5eed0007 esi=5eed0006 ebp=5eed0005 (kept: no register committed)
popad partial   sp=B-16 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+17
                  edi=51070000 esi=51070001 ebp=51070002 (CHANGED)
leave           sp=B-64 code=c0000005 np=2 i0=0 i1=B+0 ctxsp=+0 ip=+4
